  "body": "## Status\n\nA finite exact operator realization check for one family in the selected PR589 nine-stage R439 bit allocation. No new \u03ba; the selected certificate and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n\n## Finding\n\nThe deterministic maximum-multiplicity mixed-child family is `(pair=1, copy=0)`, with four helper occurrences over idle children 0 and 7. The pinned schedule and selection are rebuilt from source.\n\n- Child 0: one rank-8 helper at stage 1 plus a rank-6 idle remainder equals the source rank-14 pending map.\n- Child 7: three rank-8 helpers at stage 5 plus a rank-4 idle remainder equals the source rank-28 pending map.\n\nFor each interval, exact rational composition of `D(P) = [[I-P,P],[P,I-P]]` matches on all 128 standard basis columns. All six orders of the three mutually orthogonal child-7 helper factors agree (a positive commutation control). Four malformed-operator controls reject an omitted helper, a duplicate helper, an equal-rank wrong axis, and a wrong source port.\n\nThis extends PR1307's all-family geometric projector census with an independent matrix replay for one actual mixed-child family. It does not import PR1307's checker. PR1334 prices relaxed selected-bit levers; PR1311 treats a different PR1122 word. Neither covers this family operator identity.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/seed03-bit-physical-family/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/seed03-bit-physical-family/test_package.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/seed03-bit-physical-family\n```\n\nExpected verifier output:\n\n```text\nPASS_PR589_PHYSICAL_FAMILY pair=1 copy=0 children=0,7 helpers=4 columns=128 controls=4 orderings=6 no_new_kappa\n```\n\nThe direct verifier and focused tests passed on CPython 3.14.7. Python 3.12 was unavailable locally, so the registered Python 3.12 wrapper command was not run.\n\n## Pins and limits\n\n- Assignment: bit supplier, OS draw `2447174283`, seed `03`.\n- Exact base: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`.\n- Selected record: \u03ba `836330098538459/500000000000000000`; selected PR589 source commit `a5afc8c6169ea61ba7c51dfd3cade02cc7b13b46`.\n- PR1307 predecessor head: `4cb255ef445e2abc3ff8845fa01210b974e2cf6c`; its `RESULT.json` blob and SHA-256 are recorded in `SOURCES.json`.\n- Git blob and SHA-256 pins for all live inputs are in `research/seed03-bit-physical-family/SOURCES.json`.\n\nA final overlap refresh checked PR1345 head `b54a856aa79857d91cd5d65f8f7144e26c8c084f`, a fixed-word single/pair gate-order transport census that does not test helper placement into idle-family projectors, and PR1344 head `a42e525e9868970f3fa2d99dccca45f014aa0fd3`, a separate R439 frame-509 local matrix replay. Both are distinct from this selected physical-family address-map identity; exact URLs and heads are pinned in `SOURCES.json`.\n\nThis package checks one family's exact rational address operators under the inherited PR589 projector interpretation. It does not replay all helper scalar maps, all families, the complete interleaved caller, native lowering, all-size compilation, precision/tape, analytic transfer, or the multiplication theorem. No supplier adoption or \u03ba improvement is claimed.\n\n## Credit and disclosure\n\nCredit DreamingOfClouds and eumemic for PR589/PR555 and the retained bit supplier lineage; credit commdata2338 for PR1307's geometric census. Prepared by Cinna Davis (`@1337isnot1337`) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance for research, implementation, verification, and writing. No subagents or independent human review are claimed. New package material is Apache-2.0.\n",
